# This fixture asserts the conformant 16-octet global-only next hop. Driving
# `next-hop fe80::cafe` and asserting a 16-octet field whose only address is
# LINK-LOCAL is a shape RFC 2545 Section 3 forbids ("the global IPv6 address of
# the next hop"). Its config carries the same `local-link-local` leaf as
# conf-llnh-update.conf, so the pair varies one thing.
#
# RFC requirement: RFC2545-3-3 negative -- the link-local address is NOT included, because
# no connected prefix contains both recipient fd00::3 and the global next hop
# 2001:db8::ffff, which sits on no locally connected subnet. The asserted MP_REACH_NLRI
# is 800E26 0002 01 10 with one 16-octet address and nothing appended.
#
# This config differs from conf-llnh-update.conf in ONE variable: the route's next hop.
# Both carry `local-link-local fe80::1`, both enable the link-local-nexthop capability,
# and both use local fd00::2 and peer fd00::3 on the connected fd00::2/127 prefix.
# Explicit setup owns fd00::2/128, fd00::3/127 and fe80::1/128 on loopback. The pair
# pins inclusion to the shared-subnet condition rather than the leaf or capability.
# An encoder that always appended fails this file; one that never appended fails
# conf-llnh-update.ci.
option=file:conf-llnh-lla-only.conf
option=bind:ipv6
1:cmd:announce ipv6 unicast 2001:db8:1::1/128 next-hop 2001:db8::ffff origin igp local-preference 100
1:raw:FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF:004E02:000000374001010040020040050400000064800E260002011020010DB800000000000000000000FFFF008020010DB8000100000000000000000001
1:cmd:announce eor ipv6 unicast
1:raw:FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF:001E02:00000007900F0003000201
